{title: Spirit of God, Descend upon My Heart}
{artist: George Croly / Frederick C. Atkinson}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: C}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The United Methodist Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: United Methodist Publishing House, 1989), # 500)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Spirit of [G7]God, [C]des[F]cend up[Dm]on [G7]my [C]heart;
[Am]Wean [B7]it from [Em]earth; [A7]through [G]all [D7]its pulses [G7]move;
[G7]Stoop to my weak[F]ness, [G7]mighty as Thou art;
[C]And make me [G7]love [F]Thee [C]as I ought__[G7]__ to [C]love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Hast Thou not [G7]bid [C]me [F]love Thee, [Dm]God [G7]and [C]King?
[Am]All, [B7]all Thine [Em]own, [A7]soul, [G]heart [D7]and strength and [G7]mind.
[G7]I see Thy cross; [F]there [G7]teach my heart to cling:
[C]O let me [G7]seek [F]Thee, [C]and O let__[G7]__ me [C]find!
{end_of_verse}
